tools/binutils-2.10-dvp-ld.patch: the linker side of the DVP overlays, for
GNU binutils 2.10 (ftp.gnu.org, GPL-2.0-or-later), applied by tools/setup.sh
after tools/binutils-2.10-ee.patch.

dvp-as writes each VU microprogram overlay as a non-allocated
.DVP.overlay.<...> section and fills .DVP.ovlytab itself (name offset, EE
load address and VU address, all three as ordinary relocations), so the
table needs nothing from the linker beyond relocation. What the EE linker
adds is where the overlay sections go: every one is an orphan, and the
Cygnus "sky" ld gives each its own output section at address 0. The rule
is the one in ld/emultempl/elf32.em's place_orphan of the Cygnus
ee-gcc 2.9-991111 combined source tree (GPL, published as
github.com/polybiusproxy/parappa2_gcc, commit 620426a), which guards it for
the elf32l5900 and elf32elmip emulations; the plain build's linker is
configured mipsel-elf, whose emulation is elf32elmip. Without it ld 2.10
places a non-allocated orphan at the location counter, as every other
non-allocated section of the retail link is (MAIN.MAP: .mdebug,
.DVP.ovlytab, .DVP.ovlystrtab, .stab and .stabstr all at the end of
.vubss, the twelve overlays at 0).

Applied with `patch -p1` in the extracted binutils-2.10 tree. Nothing here
comes from an SDK.

--- a/ld/emultempl/elf32.em
+++ b/ld/emultempl/elf32.em
@@ -889,6 +889,20 @@
   const char *outsecname;
   lang_output_section_statement_type *os;
 
+#if defined (TARGET_IS_elf32l5900) || defined (TARGET_IS_elf32elmip)
+  /* A DVP overlay section gets an output section of its own at address 0:
+     its contents run from VU memory, and its load address is recorded in
+     .DVP.ovlytab.  */
+  secname = bfd_get_section_name (s->owner, s);
+  if (strncmp (secname, ".DVP.overlay.", sizeof ".DVP.overlay." - 1) == 0)
+    {
+      os = lang_output_section_statement_lookup (secname);
+      os->addr_tree = exp_intop (0);
+      wild_doit (&os->children, s, os, file);
+      return true;
+    }
+#endif
+
   if ((s->flags & SEC_ALLOC) == 0)
     return false;
 
